       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine's labeled maximum is 10 mg once daily, and 50 mg is five times that. At that dose the risks include severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged peripheral vasodilation. Your note about normal kidney and liver function doesn't change the ceiling.\n\nThis may be a typo. If you meant 5 mg, the usual starting dose, or 10 mg, the maximum, I can enter either one right away.\n\n- **5 mg PO once daily:** the standard starting dose for most adults.\n- **10 mg PO once daily:** the maximum, usually used after titration.\n\nWhich dose should I enter? If you intended something higher for a specific clinical reason, please talk with pharmacy or the prescriber. I can't enter a dose above the labeled maximum."
